From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Liminix AX6600 bringup
Date: Thu, 17 Sep 2026 00:00:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] wifi: ath11k: skip early probe until userspace is running

This device builds ath11k into the kernel, because a full-system ram
image cannot load modules (the kmodloader would have to load them from
the very derivation the image is embedded in). A built-in ath11k probes
its devices during early boot, which is the wrong time twice over:

  - the firmware is not there yet. The wifi service stages it (and reads
    this board's pre-calibration out of the eMMC ART partition) from
    userspace, the way ImmortalWrt's caldata hotplug hook does;
  - the QCN9074 does not survive being probed that early anyway: its MHI
    firmware boot fails, and the failure can leave the device stuck bound
    with a half-initialised SRNG, so a later unbind oopses in
    ath11k_ce_cleanup_pipes -> ath11k_hal_srng_access_begin.

Return -ENODEV from both probes while the kernel is still booting, which
leaves the devices unbound and available for a later probe. The
ath11k-probe service then writes the PCI address to
/sys/bus/pci/drivers_probe and the platform device name to
/sys/bus/platform/drivers_probe once the firmware service has run - the
same ordering a modular ath11k gets from being loaded at ~28s.

Signed-off-by: Liminix AX6600 bringup
---
 drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath11k/ahb.c | 14 ++++++++++++++
 drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath11k/pci.c | 10 ++++++++++
 2 files changed, 24 insertions(+)

--- a/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath11k/ahb.c
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath11k/ahb.c
@@ -5,6 +5,7 @@
  */
 
 #include <linux/module.h>
+#include <linux/kernel.h>
 #include <linux/platform_device.h>
 #include <linux/property.h>
 #include <linux/of_device.h>
@@ -1163,6 +1164,19 @@
 
 static int ath11k_ahb_probe(struct platform_device *pdev)
 {
+	/* Liminix: with the driver built into the kernel this would probe
+	 * during early boot, before the wifi service has staged the Q6
+	 * firmware and read the board's calibration out of the eMMC ART
+	 * partition. Leave the device unbound instead; the ath11k-probe
+	 * service binds it once the system is up, which is the timing a
+	 * modular ath11k gets from being loaded late.
+	 */
+	if (system_state != SYSTEM_RUNNING) {
+		dev_info(&pdev->dev, "ath11k_ahb: skip early probe (system_state=%d)\n",
+			 system_state);
+		return -ENODEV;
+	}
+
 	struct ath11k_base *ab;
 	const struct ath11k_hif_ops *hif_ops;
 	const struct ath11k_pci_ops *pci_ops;
--- a/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath11k/pci.c
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath11k/pci.c
@@ -6,6 +6,7 @@
 
 #include <linux/module.h>
 #include <linux/msi.h>
+#include <linux/kernel.h>
 #include <linux/pci.h>
 #include <linux/of.h>
 #include <linux/time.h>
@@ -956,6 +957,15 @@
 static int ath11k_pci_probe(struct pci_dev *pdev,
 			    const struct pci_device_id *pci_dev)
 {
+	/* Liminix: skip the automatic early probe; the QCN9074 RDDMs and
+	 * sticks bound, so bind it explicitly from userspace instead.
+	 */
+	if (system_state != SYSTEM_RUNNING) {
+		dev_info(&pdev->dev, "ath11k_pci: skip early probe (system_state=%d)\n",
+			 system_state);
+		return -ENODEV;
+	}
+
 	struct ath11k_base *ab;
 	struct ath11k_pci *ab_pci;
 	u32 soc_hw_version_major, soc_hw_version_minor;
